e(IC,209,212,'Software: required computer','rule',D7,'Software no longer requires a computer rank by size. Instead, program size sets the computer grade it needs. Tiny, Small, and Medium programs need a Minor computer, carry 1 or 2 Tasks, and serve a single user. Large and Huge programs need a Moderate computer, carry multiple Tasks, and serve dozens of users at once. Colossal programs need a Major computer and serve hundreds of users at once. Computer rank no longer limits program size; it only caps Task target numbers. A Task runs at its own TN or the computer rank\'s maximum TN, whichever is lower. Replace every "Required Computer Rank" in program stat blocks with the matching Required Computer Grade.',
  [(None,'Software requirement','Required Computer Rank (by size)','Required Computer Grade (by size)'),(None,'Task TN on a lower-rank computer','not allowed','runs at the computer rank\'s max TN')])
